WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:06.880
Think of the BRI as both a massive trade

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.520
network

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.600
and a political vision. It started with a

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.000
speech that President Xi Jinping made

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.080
back in Kazakhstan in 2013.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.159
He talked about building a new trade

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.159
route based on the old Silk Road —

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:24.960
an ancient network that linked Asia, the

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.479
Middle East and Europe for almost

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.720
2,000 years. 

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.159
The Belt and Road Initiative basically

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:51.680
weaves together lots of projects.

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:53.360
It could be China building things from

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.240
scratch, upgrading existing

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.119
infrastructure,

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.960
handing out loans or making investments.

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:00.880
There are overland routes that connect

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.479
China to central and south Asia, the

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.719
Middle East and Europe.

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.640
That's the "belt". It includes what's

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:07.360
called the China-Pakistan Economic

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.360
Corridor

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.959
where around $60 billion are

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.239
being spent on things like coal and

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:14.879
hydro power plants,

00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:17.599
wind farms, highways and a new high-speed

00:02:14.879 --> 00:02:19.599
rail link between Peshawar and Karachi.

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:21.440
Then there's the "road" part which is

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:23.040
slightly confusing because it actually

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.680
refers to a maritime

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.879
Silk Road — sea routes that connect China

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.440
to Southeast Asia,

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:31.760
Africa and Europe. It includes major

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:34.000
investments in ports across the world — 

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.760
places like Sri Lanka, Dubai, Djibouti,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.760
Greece and Spain. Even as far as Peru.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.959
Now we listed some of the big examples

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.360
but BRI

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:53.200
specifics are hard to come by. There's

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.720
actually no confirmed list of everything

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.360
and everyone involved

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.840
but it's estimated to include 2,600

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.599
projects in more than 100 countries.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.120
And that makes it hard to come up with

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:05.519
an accurate price tag.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:19.680
So what's the endgame here? Well, for

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:22.800
China the BRI is obviously about trade.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.080
But all this global interconnectedness

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:42.000
and the huge amount of money involved

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.080
means the Belt and Road Initiative is

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.440
also political. 

00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:12.239
By building all this stuff China is also

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:14.319
exporting its version

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:16.239
of economic development. Now, the way the

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:18.320
West has usually done it is to provide

00:04:16.239 --> 00:04:19.040
economic support but with conditions

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.680
attached

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.800
like certain democratic reforms. China's

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.560
style is different.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.280
The World Bank reckons that China's BRI

00:04:42.639 --> 00:04:45.440
projects

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.800
could lift more than 7 million people

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:48.800
out of extreme poverty

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:51.520
and that transport projects could boost

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:52.800
global trade by up to 6.2%.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.199
And, of course, there are lots of

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:58.160
countries eager to take China's money.

00:04:55.199 --> 00:05:00.320
Djibouti is one example. Its BRI projects

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:02.320
include a major port, a new railway line

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.280
to the Ethiopian capital and a gas

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.840
pipeline.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.680
China's put up around $14 billion 

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.240
in investments and loans for Djibouti

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.960
between 2012 and 2020.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:14.479
But there are risks — like corruption.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:16.880
Especially because there's so much

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:17.600
secrecy surrounding most of these BRI

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:20.160
deals.

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:38.000
So,

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:39.759
it's politicians making these deals

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.600
and there are plenty of examples of

00:05:39.759 --> 00:05:43.759
ordinary people losing out.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.720
Another thing to remember is that with

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:53.680
all the talk of Chinese money funding

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.600
these projects

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:57.759
it's often more accurate to say that

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.840
it's actually Chinese loans.

00:05:57.759 --> 00:06:01.440
And that creates another risk — that some

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:04.479
countries could be taking on

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:06.160
too much debt. Remember Djibouti? It's

00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:08.880
facing what the World Bank calls

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:11.199
"debt distress". Its debt to China amounts

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.240
to 70% of its GDP.

00:06:11.199 --> 00:06:16.400
And look at Sri Lanka.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:18.479
Former President Mahinda Rajapaksa

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.520
borrowed billions to develop a massive

00:06:18.479 --> 00:06:21.280
new port.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.440
When Sri Lanka struggled to pay back the

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:25.759
money it ended up with a new deal

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.440
that gave China control of the port for

00:06:25.759 --> 00:06:29.680
99 years.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:31.840
That led to accusations that the loans

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.319
compromised Sri Lanka's sovereignty,

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:36.080
which China denies. 

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.840
But it's this kind of thing that's

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.800
led to some people calling the Belt and

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.520
Road Initiative

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.160
a "debt trap for vulnerable countries".

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:59.280
Others

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:03.280
disagree. 

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:06.720
And

00:07:05.919 --> 00:07:08.960
it seems

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:10.720
this success has got Western powers,

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.580
especially the United States,

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:15.199
paying more attention.

00:07:15.199 --> 00:07:18.720
At the recent G7 summit they set out

00:07:17.759 --> 00:07:20.240
their own plan,

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.319
complete with its own snazzy

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.120
abbreviation — B3W

00:07:22.319 --> 00:07:26.400
which stands for Build Back Better World.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.440
They're emphasizing things like

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.280
transparency,

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:31.120
good governance, the environment and

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:32.400
bringing in the private sector to help

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:35.520
fund it all.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:36.080
But B3W is thin on details. There's no

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:38.560
budget

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:40.400
and no timetable. 

00:08:11.599 --> 00:08:15.840
Now, one way to

00:08:14.639 --> 00:08:17.840
look at all this

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.879
is that it's another area of competition

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:21.199
between China

00:08:18.879 --> 00:08:22.960
and the West. 

00:08:32.159 --> 00:08:36.800
But maybe

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.959
there's another way to look at it.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.320
If China and the West are competing that

00:08:38.959 --> 00:08:42.800
could give more choice,

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:44.560
more opportunity and crucially more

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:45.839
money to developing countries that

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.320
desperately need it.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.000
The Belt and Road Initiative is about

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.080
China's position in the world.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.920
It's their strategy to outshine everyone

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.839
on the international stage.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:23.440
But some countries really don't like the

00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:26.320
idea of the Chinese

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.320
calling the shots.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:31.200
If you want to know more there are lots

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.880
of reports from Al Jazeera

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:34.800
correspondents about Belt and Road

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.560
projects from around the world.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:45.920
You can find those on YouTube or on our

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:45.920
website. See you next week.

